        {
          "id": 2255591232,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Fair enough. I know in the frame they are encoded differently, but `tvb_get_fle()` does put zero in the return value and NULL and 0 can only be distinguished using the Boolean.  So perhaps NULL should be tested for in more places.\n\nIt appears in practice that when there is no recent insert ID that MySQL encodes zero there instead of NULL (as it arguably should?), which is presumably why zero was ignored before.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
